@startuml InquiryUserRole

title Inquiry User Role API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Inquiry User Role Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "t_user_role" as t_user_role
end box

user -> page: Read user roles with optional filters and pagination
activate page
    page -> api: GET v1/author/user/role (Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp; query only)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**InquiryUserRoleQueryHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate query/header/body and checked pagination (400) -> verify JWT/roles (401) -> begin
                read-only repeatable-read transaction -> fresh now/expiry -> joined current credential/user (401) -> claims
                permission (403) -> count -> optional page -> complete mapping -> COMMIT -> 200. Every post-BEGIN rejection
                rolls back.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate UTC timestamp, known single query keys/no body, UUID id, positive signed Int64 pages/default 1/10/pageSize <=100 and ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED filter
            note over app, infra
                Reject unknown/repeated keys and malformed header/query with 400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId if
                omitted. Supplied id/userId/roleId is a non-empty UUID, never null; omitted ones are typed SQL NULL
                (filterUserId, filterRoleId). pageIndex/pageSize are positive signed 64-bit integers, default 1/10 only when
                omitted, pageSize at most 100. Compute checked offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize and reject parse/offset
                overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT with 400. Explicit empty/null-like values do not become defaults. Row
                status must be one of ACTIVE, INACTIVE, LOCKED, ARCHIVED.
            end note
            app -> app: Compute checked offset = (pageIndex - 1) * pageSize; reject numeric/offset overflow beyond nonnegative BIGINT
            alt Invalid input or pagination overflow
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roleIds/name array
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this inquiry
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                    page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
            app -> app: Bind omitted id/filterUserId/filterRoleId/rowStatus as typed SQL NULL; supplied filters are bound values
            app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
            note over app, infra
                Verify Bearer JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured roles before BEGIN. roles must be
                an array including [], every role object has UUID roleId and non-empty string name, and roleIds are unique.
                Missing/malformed roles is generic 401 E10002, never an empty-list or live-grant fallback. Derive
                callerUserId only from verified sub and accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact JWT; do not accept caller
                ids or isPlatformAdmin flags from requests.
                Require matching token hash/caller id, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now;
                missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched credentials is generic 401 E10002 with rollback before user-role
                reads. No user/role/token locks or writes. This current credential gate preserves immediate logout/reset
                revocation (Q13).
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Read and mapping work completes
                note over app, infra
                    No locks or writes. Credentials, user role count and page use one repeatable-read snapshot.
                    Timeout or unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure may interrupt any step; no partial response.
                end note
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before joined credential read; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired before fresh credential read
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload current grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this inquiry
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to read user roles.
                        api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                        page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get total items
                infra -> t_user_role: QUERY - Get total items
                activate t_user_role
                    note right of t_user_role
                        SELECT
                            COUNT(ur.id) as total_items
                        FROM author.t_user_role ur
                        INNER JOIN authen.m_user u
                            ON u.id = ur.user_id
                        INNER JOIN author.m_role r
                            ON r.id = ur.role_id
                        WHERE ur.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR ur.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.filterUserId>' IS NULL OR ur.user_id = '<sequence.filterUserId>') -- only when userId is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.filterRoleId>' IS NULL OR ur.role_id = '<sequence.filterRoleId>') -- only when roleId is specified
                        AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR ur.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                    end note
                    t_user_role -> infra: Return totalItems for non-DELETED user roles and all nullable filters
                deactivate t_user_role
                infra -> app: Return totalItems for non-DELETED user roles and all nullable filters
                app -> app: totalPages = 0 when totalItems=0, otherwise integer quotient plus nonzero remainder; no floating point or overflowing count+pageSize-1
                alt totalItems = 0
                    app -> app: items = []; skip page query; totalPages = 0
                else totalItems > 0
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get user roles
                    infra -> t_user_role: QUERY - Get user roles
                    activate t_user_role
                        note right of t_user_role
                            SELECT
                                ur.id as user_role_id,
                                ur.user_id,
                                u.display_name,
                                ur.role_id,
                                r.name as role_name,
                                ur.row_status
                            FROM author.t_user_role ur
                            INNER JOIN authen.m_user u
                                ON u.id = ur.user_id
                            INNER JOIN author.m_role r
                                ON r.id = ur.role_id
                            WHERE ur.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR ur.id = '<sequence.id>') -- only when id is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.filterUserId>' IS NULL OR ur.user_id = '<sequence.filterUserId>') -- only when userId is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.filterRoleId>' IS NULL OR ur.role_id = '<sequence.filterRoleId>') -- only when roleId is specified
                            AND ('<sequence.rowStatus>' IS NULL OR ur.row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>') -- only when rowStatus is specified
                            ORDER BY r.name, u.display_name, ur.id
                            LIMIT '<sequence.pageSize>' OFFSET '<sequence.offset>'
                        end note
                        t_user_role -> infra: Return six-field user role rows in role name/user display name/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    deactivate t_user_role
                    infra -> app: Return six-field user role rows in role name/user display name/id order from identical filters/snapshot
                    app -> app: Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0, totalItems-offset)); mismatch is internal failure
                    alt Page contains rows
                        app -> app: Map exactly userRoleId/userId/userDisplayName/roleId/roleName/rowStatus per row; required values non-null; exclude caller/assignment/token/hash/audit
                    else Page beyond range contains no rows
                        app -> app: items = []; retain positive totalItems/totalPages; no 404
                    end
                end
                app -> app: data = exactly items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages; echo validated page values; explicit empty arrays; finish full mapping
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed consistent read-only user role page
                note over app, infra
                    Approved by the product owner (answered through the lead SA, 2026-11-06; claims basis A12); use exact
                    PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT role claims under [owner-confirmed
                    review](../../../../../docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-07-api-review-design.md), Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13. This detailed
                    revision remains in-review; no backend/schema implementation.
                    The four nullable filters id/userId/roleId/rowStatus disable only themselves and combine by AND; every
                    supplied value is bound and never interpolated into SQL. userId returns the roles of that user, roleId the
                    users that have that role; the id filter is still filtered/paginated, not an unpaged alternate path. The
                    inner joins to the user and the role never remove a row because both references are mandatory foreign keys;
                    the user and the role status are not filtered.
                    After current credentials pass, authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT
                    roles. Valid roles=[] or any other role name is 403 E10009 `You do not have permission to read user roles.`
                    after rollback and before count/page SQL. Never query current caller role assignments to grant, remove or
                    replace authorization. Grant withdrawal after token issuance leaves the old privilege usable until access
                    expiry (Q4); refresh reloads current grants (Q7). User-role data returned below comes from the database
                    snapshot, distinct from author/me's calling-token snapshot.
                    Count first and optionally fetch the page in the same read-only repeatable-read snapshot as credentials.
                    Both user-role queries use identical joins and non-DELETED/id/userId/roleId/rowStatus WHERE predicates;
                    every supplied value is bound, including pageSize and checked offset. If totalItems=0 skip the page SQL and
                    return items=[], totalPages=0. With positive count, query the requested page; an offset beyond the range
                    returns items=[] with positive totals/pages and no 404. A missing/DELETED id is the same empty-list 200 for
                    an authorized caller; permission is checked before revealing whether any user role exists.
                    Rows with rowStatus DELETED are never returned. Omitted rowStatus preserves every non-DELETED status;
                    supplied status accepts only ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED. Sort by role name, then user display name,
                    then id ascending, preserving database collation. This is deterministic within one snapshot; later requests
                    may see newly committed changes and are not a frozen paging cursor.
                    Map each row to exactly userRoleId/userId/userDisplayName/roleId/roleName/rowStatus (userDisplayName is
                    plain text, null when not set). No caller id, assignment, token/hash, audit or extra table fields are
                    returned. Return exactly five data keys: items/pageIndex/pageSize/totalItems/totalPages, with explicit empty
                    arrays. Echo validated pages and compute totalPages by integer quotient/remainder (zero when count=0),
                    avoiding floating point or overflowing count+pageSize-1. Require page row count = min(pageSize, max(0,
                    totalItems-offset)); mismatch or malformed/null/missing required data is internal failure.
                    Map the full response before COMMIT, then HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry User Role Success. An unexpected
                    SQL/result/mapping error rolls back and returns generic 500 without bizCode; timeout before COMMIT rolls
                    back and returns 408 E90001. Never return partially mapped rows, mutate
                    assignments/users/roles/tokens/audit, or answer 404/409 for this inquiry.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry User Role Success; all five pagination keys
                api -> page: Show authorized user role page and totals
                page -> user: Display user roles or empty page
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Show failure without a partial user role page
                page -> user: Display failure; no user role data
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
